   "etymology": "From Old Albanian nja, from Proto-Albanian *nyá-, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *myá-, from Proto-Indo-European *smiyo- (“a, an”), from Proto-Indo-European *s(e)mih₂ or Proto-Indo-European *smiyah₂. Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *sem- (“together, one”). According to Neri, the etymology connecting një to *h₁óynos is problematic, as it assumes an unknown pronomial element at the initial sound and also does not explain the stem *nyá- without a final nasal.",
